      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Manifestations of the dynamics of defensive conditioning were studied in the cat sensorimotor cortical units. It has been shown that the process of learning is linked to the dynamics of the amount of total and useful information present in the evoked spike responses to a conditioned stimulus. As the pairings continue, the amount of useful information increases in reactions to conditioned or unconditioned stimuli and in the period preceding the conditioned stimulation."},
